' ================================================================
' Semantic cross-package arrows (tell the data-flow story)
' ================================================================
' Current model
AgentRuntime -up-> Agent        : "dispatches to"
Agent        -up-> RuntimeRef   : "bind() then reply via"
RunContext   -up-> Agent        : "threaded into on_message"
Checkpoint   ..>   Agent        : "save_state / load_state"

' New model (Stage 0 targets)
DurableAgent -up-> EventLog     : "folds log to rebuild state on wake"
Inbox        ..>   DurableAgent : "drain() becomes inbox arg in run()"
Scheduler    ..>   DurableAgent : "leases run, triggers wake"

' ToolInvoker (L1) needs these kernel contracts
ToolInvoker  -up-> ArtifactStore   : "offloads large results"
ToolInvoker  -up-> ApprovalHandler : "HITL gate (risk check)"
ToolInvoker  -up-> ToolRegistry    : "lookup + dispatch"

' ================================================================
' Notes -- ALL outside package blocks
' ================================================================

note right of AgentRuntime
  <b>GAP 1 -- God-object must split</b>
  8 methods: send_message, publish_message,
  register_agent, register, subscribe,
  unsubscribe, start, stop.
  Plan: split into 5 focused contracts:
  EventLog + Inbox + FollowGraph
  + Scheduler + SignalBus.
  RuntimeRef in message.py has the SAME
  send/publish pair -- that duplication
  dissolves when agents reply via
  DurableContext (L1), not by holding
  a runtime reference.
end note

note right of Agent
  <b>GAP 2 -- Synchronous contract cannot scale</b>
  on_message(ctx: MessageContext, payload) -> reply
  is synchronous request/reply in one call.
  Cannot survive a process crash, multi-day
  HITL pause, or worker migration.
  DurableAgent.run(ctx: DurableContext, inbox)
  replaces it completely. No coexistence path --
  this is a full kernel break.
end note

note right of Checkpoint
  <b>GAP 3 -- State authority shift</b>
  Checkpoint is currently THE source of truth.
  save_state / load_state are core Agent methods.
  Plan: EventLog is truth; state = fold(log).
  Checkpoint demotes to log-compaction snapshot.
  save_state / load_state go away entirely
  when Agent is replaced by DurableAgent.
end note

note right of RunContext
  <b>GAP 4 -- run_id not first-class</b>
  run_id is buried in Supervision.run_id,
  and Supervision is optional on RunContext.
  Plan needs run_id directly on RunContext.
  Fix: add run_id: str = "" field;
  populate from supervision.run_id when present;
  generate a fresh ULID for standalone().
end note

note right of Event
  <b>NAMING CONFLICT 1 -- events.py vs runtime/events.py</b>
  events.py Event = generic pub/sub envelope
  (type, source, schema_version, correlation_id, data).
  Plan's RunEvent = event-sourced run log entry
  (run_id, seq, kind, payload, ts).
  COMPLETELY different things.
  Rename plan's RunEvent to RunLogEntry
  to eliminate confusion.
end note

note right of GraphStore
  <b>NAMING CONFLICT 2 -- graph.py vs runtime/graph.py</b>
  graph.py GraphStore = RAG knowledge graph
  (Entity, Relationship, SubGraph, CypherCapable).
  Plan's SubscriptionGraph = agent social follow-graph.
  COMPLETELY different things.
  Rename plan's contract to FollowGraph
  (already done in this diagram).
end note

note right of ToolInvoker
  <b>GAP 5 -- ToolInvoker not yet implemented</b>
  All needed kernel contracts ARE present:
  ToolRegistry, ApprovalHandler,
  ArtifactStore, ChainPolicy.
  Still missing: bridge transport + sandbox
  prelude (L2 capabilities) + ToolChainTool.
  ToolInvoker itself = first thing to write at L1.
end note

@enduml
